\title{Constructuve proof of infinite nonsquares}
\date{2026-03-07T19:22:24Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Here is a different proof:}

\proof{
  Let #{n} be an arbitrary natural number, and consider the number #{(n+1)^2 + 1}.  Clearly #{(n+1)^2 + 1 > n}.  Since #{(n+1)^2} is a square greater than zero, [the lemma](008X) tells us that #{(n+1)^2 + 1} is not a square.
}

\p{Unlike the previous proof, this proof directly tells us how to calculate, for any #{n}, a bigger number which is not a square.}

